.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH SPT-BENCHMARK 1  "benchmark " 
.SH NAME
benchmark \- Controlled benchmarking against forwards
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbenchmark\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Controlled benchmarking against forwards
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
benchmark\-run(1)
End\-to\-end mixed workload
.TP
benchmark\-latency(1)
Latency\-focused benchmark
.TP
benchmark\-throughput(1)
Throughput\-focused benchmark
.TP
benchmark\-udp(1)
UDP benchmark (SSH3 only)
.TP
benchmark\-reconnect(1)
Reconnect benchmark
.TP
benchmark\-dns(1)
DNS benchmark
.TP
benchmark\-limits(1)
Limit/throttle introspection
.TP
benchmark\-report(1)
Report tooling
.TP
benchmark\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  spt benchmark run \-\-profile edge \-\-forward db \-\-duration 30s \-\-connections 16
  spt benchmark latency \-\-profile edge \-\-forward db \-\-samples 1000
  spt benchmark throughput \-\-profile edge \-\-forward db \-\-duration 60s \-\-payload\-size 64KiB
  spt benchmark report compare \-\-baseline base.json \-\-candidate cand.json
  spt benchmark report export \-\-format markdown \-\-out report.md
